<!-- ============ FAQ ============ -->
<section class="section" style="padding-bottom: 80px;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Frequently Asked Questions</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Everything you need to know.</h2>
    </div>
    <div style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          How does Teamwork Commerce track individual jewelry pieces?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Every piece receives a unique Electronic Product Code (EPC) via RFID — its own digital passport. The unit control ledger tracks each item's full history: when it was received, which display case it's in, when it was viewed by an associate, when it left for consignment, and when it was sold. RFID handhelds can count an entire case of 50 items in seconds without handling a single piece.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          Does Teamwork Commerce handle repairs and appraisals?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Teamwork Commerce is not a jewelry-specific POS with deep repair ticketing or appraisal management. For independent jewelers with heavy repair workflows, dedicated platforms like WJewel or Jewel360 may be a better fit. Teamwork is built for multi-location jewelry chains and luxury brands that need enterprise infrastructure: RFID serialization, omnichannel fulfillment, global compliance, AI clienteling, and SOC 2 security — capabilities that jewelry-specific POS platforms don't offer.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          Can Teamwork handle consignment and deposit transactions?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. The platform supports deposit collection for custom orders and layaway, with automatic balance tracking and customer notifications. For consignment, personal shoppers can take RFID-tracked inventory for clients to try at home, with full chain-of-custody visibility. Every piece is accounted for at every step.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          How secure is the platform for high-value inventory?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Teamwork Commerce is SOC 2 Type 2 certified, GDPR compliant, and PCI DSS compliant. Role-based permissions control who can access cases, process transactions, and view customer data. Full audit trails log every item interaction — views, case opens, transactions, and whitelisting. EAS gate integration with blacklist/whitelist prevents theft at exits.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          Is Teamwork Commerce built for multi-location jewelry chains?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. Teamwork Commerce is enterprise retail infrastructure for jewelry and watch chains, including a globally recognized fine jewelry house that we are unable to name publicly. Capabilities include RFID serialization that tracks each piece as its own unit, integrated OMS for omnichannel fulfilment, SOC 2 Type 2, PCI DSS and GDPR compliance, and localization in 40+ countries with multi-currency support — so expanding into a new market is not a re-platform.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

